  the provider never documents into a contract every provider shares, and the base is configuration
  rather than provider knowledge.
- **F9's action set deliberately differs from F7's on two points, and F8 will meet both.**
  `AcceptDisputeAction` is withheld even though ConnexPay's portal offers "Accept Chargeback": nothing
  in the CMS payload says whether the portal would take one on *this* case, an acceptance is the one
  irreversible act in this domain, and withholding costs nothing because the link lands the operator
  on the case. And `SUBMITTED` is **not** consulted when deciding whether the case is still ours,
  unlike at Stripe — there it means an API call of ours filed the response, here it means an operator
